      "history_summaries": [
        "Round 1/3: Fixed `ackA_implies_reqA` / `ackB_implies_reqB` / `ackC_implies_reqC` assertion failures. Error type: dut_bug. Root cause: Controller BUSY state kept `ackReg` asserted until `!io.req` was detected, but due to register-update semantics, when the client drops `reqReg` on the same clock edge, the controller reads the old `io.req` value (1) and fails to deassert `ackReg` for one extra cycle, creating a window where `io.ack=1` and `io.req=0`. Fix: added unconditional `ackReg := false.B` at the top of the BUSY state (arbiter.scala:94). The ack signal only needs to be high for the single cycle where the client samples it to transition REQ→HAVE_TOKEN (controller sets ackReg in READY, client reads it on the next clock edge). Clearing ackReg immediately in BUSY eliminates the one-cycle stale-ack window. All structurally identical controller instances (controllerA/B/C) share the same Controller class, so all three `ack*_implies_req*` assertions are repaired homologously. Assertion labels preserved unchanged.",
        "Round 2/3: Fix mutex_passTokens (and cascading req*_eventually_ack* liveness). Error type: dut_bug. Root cause: Controller.passTokenReg initialized to true.B for all three controller instances (line 69), causing all three passToken signals to be high simultaneously at reset, violating mutual exclusion. Fix: changed passTokenReg initialization to `RegInit(if (id == Selection.A) true.B else false.B)`, so only controllerA starts with the token. This addresses the causal path: the mutual exclusion property checks that at most one passToken is true; initializing all three to true.B creates an immediate violation at time 0 before any clock edge. With only controllerA holding the token, the arbiter can start cycling from A through the round-robin sequence, enabling controllers B and C to eventually receive the token and service their clients, which also resolves the req*_eventually_ack* liveness failures. No homologous assertions exist because the fix targets the single `RegInit(true.B)` on line 69 in the shared Controller class. All assertion labels preserved unchanged.",
        "Round 3/3: Fix reqA_eventually_ackA / reqB_eventually_ackB / reqC_eventually_ackC liveness failures. Error type: dut_bug. Root cause: In Controller IDLE state, the `.otherwise` clause (when not selected) unconditionally cleared `passTokenReg := false.B` (line 88). This destroyed the token whenever the token-holding controller was not the currently selected one by the round-robin arbiter. Since `active = passTokenA || passTokenB || passTokenC`, clearing any passToken caused all three to become zero, freezing the arbiter at Selection.X (deadlock). Fix: removed the `.otherwise { passTokenReg := false.B }` clause entirely. When not selected, passTokenReg now retains its previous value, letting the token persist until intentionally consumed (servicing a request, IDLE+selected+req→READY, line 83) or passed (BUSY+!req→IDLE, line 100). All three controllers share the same Controller class, so the fix applies homologously to all three req*_eventually_ack* assertions. All assertion labels preserved unchanged."
      ],
